Zenith patch 0002: native callbacks for extensions (RenderingDevice.native_callback_add).

PR #114670 runs a script callback at the upscale point, but upscaler libraries (AMD FSR, NVIDIA DLSS) record
their work into the engine's own command list, which no bound API hands out. This binds the engine's
driver_callback_add (as MetalFX uses it) for extensions: a C function run with the native command list at its
place in the render graph, the D3D12 device and queue, and each handed texture's ID3D12Resource with the state
(legacy barriers) or layout (enhanced barriers) it is in. Legacy barriers: the textures are moved to the states
their usages ask for first. After the callback the D3D12 driver forgets its cached command-list state
(descriptor heaps, root signatures, pipelines, dynamic state). D3D12 only; other drivers report version 0.
Zenith's own work, vendor-free, MIT like Godot.

